     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release tops out at 2,000 to 2,500 mg/day. A dose of 5,100 mg/day would greatly raise the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, in which case please tell me the dose and frequency\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose is above the usual maximum."
      }
     ],
